 "notes": "Plan of the 10 m DiveWorld dive tower: entry from the floating pontoon (flonder) or the stairs, shelves at 1.4 m and 5 m, a platform at 9 m on the 10 m floor, a small boat, two red rings and the cenote-style rock wall. Platform depths 1.4/5/9 m are from diveworld.nl and René Magazine; which grey shelf is 1.4 m and which is 5 m, and the object identities, are assumptions. The tower diameter (13 m) is derived from the published 1.3 million litres at 10 m depth, and north is not known; all positions are approximate.",
